# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets, key material and data dumps  (SEC-002, SEC-011)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quadlet environment files hold CHAUDRON_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY and provider
# API keys in clear text. They belong in $HOME on the host, never in the repo.
*.env
!.env.example
chaudron.env
chaudron-db.env

# Key material, in any of the shapes it usually takes
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets/
.secrets/

# Database dumps: a Chaudron dump is a full inventory of someone's home, plus the
# encrypted provider credentials. Keep them out of the working tree entirely.
*.sql
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.dump.gz
!backend/migrations/**/*.sql
dumps/
backups/

# Open Food Facts local dataset (ADR-0008): gigabytes, and ODbL-licensed
data/openfoodfacts/
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz

# Receipt images and user uploads — personal data, never versioned.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is not tidiness. Unanchored, `receipts/`
# matches a directory of that name at *any* depth, and it silently swallowed
# `frontend/src/features/receipts/` — six source files that existed locally,
# built locally, and were simply absent from the repository. The failure surfaced
# on CI as `Cannot find module '../receipts/ReceiptsScreen'`, which points at the
# importer rather than at the rule that removed the import's target.
#
# A pattern that hides source code is worse than one that misses a data
# directory: the second is caught by review, the first is caught by whoever
# clones the repository next.
/uploads/
/media/
/receipts/
data/uploads/
data/media/
data/receipts/

# Local demo stack (see docs/screenshots): generated, never committed
frontend/.env.local
